  "description": "ZEZVEJ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C106 H112 Ho8 N12 O40,2(C2 H6 O1),2(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 6 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 6 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho1A (Ho) has 6 O neighbors; Ho2A (Ho) has 6 O neighbors; Ho3A (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho4A (Ho) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.495-3.872 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.88-112.77°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C112H124Cl4Ho8N12O42. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
